course: dictionary
lesson: 13790
title: Big words for big floods
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Inundation» is a formal word for a flood: water covers land that is usually dry. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues. «After three days of heavy rain, the river spread over the fields in a great inundation.» The rain and the water covering the fields tell you it means a flood.
explain: The word can also mean a very large amount of things arriving at once. «The post office had an inundation of letters before Christmas.» Lots of letters arriving together, so it means a huge number, not water.
explain: Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about water, or about lots of things arriving? Then try a simpler word in its place. If «flood» fits, your meaning is right. «Inundation» is formal, so you will often find it in serious writing and geography books.
fact: Inundation means a flood, when water covers land that is usually dry.
fact: Inundation can also mean a very large amount of things arriving at once, as in «an inundation of letters.»
fact: The word «inundation» is formal; in everyday talk people often say «flood».
fact: In ancient Egypt, the Nile's yearly inundation covered the fields with water and left rich black mud that helped crops grow.
fact: A good check is to swap in «flood» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «After the heavy rain, an inundation covered the fields.» What does inundation mean here? | A bridge built over a river | A small puddle in the playground | *A flood, when water covers land that is usually dry | A long dry spell with no rain at all
exercise: «The shop had an inundation of phone calls on the first morning.» What does inundation mean in this sentence? | A loud and sudden noise | *A very large amount of things arriving all at once | A broken phone | One quiet phone call
exercise: «Every spring the Nile's inundation left rich black mud on the fields.» Which word tells you that water covered the fields? | *Inundation | Rich | Spring | Black
test: «The town was cut off by the inundation after three days of rain.» What is the inundation? | A fast train | *A flood | A new road into town | A sunny day at the seaside
test: «Our inbox was hit by an inundation of spam emails.» What does inundation suggest? | A flood of water in the office | A tiny note on the desk | *A huge amount arriving all at once | A single quiet message
exam: Which sentence uses inundation to mean a flood? | Our class had an inundation of spelling tests. | *After the storm, an inundation covered the farm fields. | The shop had an inundation of customers on Saturday.
